<title>NEW ZEALAND: Govt Property to make NZ$50 mln bond issue - ANZ.</title>
<headline>Govt Property to make NZ$50 mln bond issue - ANZ.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANZ Banking Group (New Zealand) Ltd said on Friday that Government Property Services Ltd was about to undertake a NZ$50 million bond issue.</p>
<p>The bonds mature on February 15, 2001, and have an eight percent coupon.  </p>
<p>They will be offered at a margin of 0.85 percent over the underlying New Zealand Government bond rate.</p>
<p>ANZ Banking Group NZ is the arranger of the issue.</p>
<p>Subscriptions open on March 10, with rate-set occuring on March 13 and settlement on March 17.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
